 ## Overview
-OTS+SAtn Densification is a density control strategy adapted from the OTS+SAtn splatting technique to operate within the standard 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) framework for real-world scene reconstruction [S1]. It addresses unbounded primitive growth by imposing strict caps on the total number of Gaussians and adapting densification thresholds to match 3DGS conventions [S1]. Unlike standard 3DGS which may allow indefinite growth, this method stops densification once a predefined maximum count (e.g., 100k, 500k, 1m, or 5m) is reached, ensuring controlled memory usage while maintaining competitive reconstruction quality [S1].
